{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607/events","html_url":"https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/16607","id":2371970107,"node_id":"I_kwDOAB_CCc6NYWQ7","number":16607,"title":"Should we deprecate `LevMarLSQFitter`?","user":{"login":"Cadair","id":1391051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTEwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1391051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair","html_url":"https://github.com/Cadair","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cadair/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":35800382,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNTgwMDM4Mg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/labels/modeling","name":"modeling","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":null},{"id":1345152042,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzQ1MTUyMDQy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/labels/API%20change","name":"API change","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"PRs and issues that change an existing API, possibly requiring a deprecation period"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2024-06-25T07:57:48Z","updated_at":"2024-07-05T03:11:33Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"We have two implementations of the Levenberg-Marquardt fitting algortihm [LevMarLSQFitter](https://docs.astropy.org/en/stable/api/astropy.modeling.fitting.LevMarLSQFitter.html#astropy.modeling.fitting.LevMarLSQFitter) and [LMLSQFitter](https://docs.astropy.org/en/stable/api/astropy.modeling.fitting.LMLSQFitter.html#astropy.modeling.fitting.LMLSQFitter). The latter uses a newer function in scipy [`least_squares`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.least_squares.html) and the former uses the older [`leastsq`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.leastsq.html).

It's exceptionally not-obvious from the documentation why you might choose one over the other, in fact, I had to spend a good couple of minutes figuring out which was which and I *knew* one was a newer implementation in scipy.

I am sure there are still a lot of uses of the old one in the wild, so deprecating it might be tricky, but perhaps we could make an extra long deprecation period or something. Or at least explicitly recommend the newer one in the docs?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/comments/2209912659","html_url":"https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/16607#issuecomment-2209912659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/16607","id":2209912659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB_CCc6DuJdT","user":{"login":"WilliamJamieson","id":20687711,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg3NzEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20687711?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson","html_url":"https://github.com/WilliamJamieson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WilliamJamieson/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-07-05T03:11:32Z","updated_at":"2024-07-05T03:11:32Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"My intention was to eventually deprecate it. However, if it becomes a maintenance issue I can see having it alias the `LMLSQFitter`. They should agree up to some minor numerical differences except when having bounded parameter values. The question is how to go about informing users of the tiny change.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/comments/2209912659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}}

