{"action":"closed","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/15311","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/15311/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/15311/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/issues/15311/events","html_url":"https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/15311","id":1894165981,"node_id":"I_kwDOAB_CCc5w5q3d","number":15311,"title":"Use of timezone in Time.datetime","user":{"login":"mhvk","id":2789820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODk4MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2789820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk","html_url":"https://github.com/mhvk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhvk/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":181675,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxODE2NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/labels/Feature%20Request","name":"Feature Request","color":"bfdadc","default":false,"description":null},{"id":10515381,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUxNTM4MQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/astropy/labels/time","name":"time","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2023-09-13T09:51:05Z","updated_at":"2023-09-13T13:16:12Z","closed_at":"2023-09-13T13:16:12Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### What is the problem this feature will solve?

Python in trying to move away from `datetime` that have not explicitly set a timezone, raising warning for, e.g., `datetime.utcnow()` which caused problems for our tests for python 3.12 (see #14784 and the discussion in #15298). This may mean that output from `time.to_datetime()` by default produces output that cannot easily be calculated with.

### Describe the desired outcome

To at least communicate that our `scale="utc"` times have `timezone="utc"`, i.e., make `TimeDatetime` as informative as possible. For `scale="utc"`, it could set `timezone="utc"` (if no explicit timezone is given by calling `to_datetime(timezone)`, for other scales it still only makes sense to use `timezone=None`.

EDIT: in principle, we could also store any timezone the user has given on `Time`, but this would seem to add a lot of complexity for little benefit for anything astronomers actually need `Time` for.

### Additional context

The actual change would be rather minimal. From https://github.com/astropy/astropy/pull/15298#discussion_r1321872301, it would require changes at https://github.com/astropy/astropy/blob/bde1b85647a27a83f57d80d891c106e219d15a0b/astropy/time/formats.py#L1126-L1130

Essentially, one would change those lines to,
```
        if self._scale == "utc":
            if timezone is None:
                timezone = timezone.utc
        else:
            if timezone is not None:
                raise ScaleValueError(
                    f"scale is {self._scale}, must be 'utc' when timezone is supplied."
                )
```
